## How it works

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[yfinance: sector tickers + benchmark] --> B[Technical indicators<br/>SMA, EMA, RSI, Bollinger, momentum, vol]
    B --> C[Chronological train/test split<br/>per asset]
    C --> D[Train RF / SVM / DNN<br/>report out-of-sample accuracy]
    D --> E[Backtest on held-out period only<br/>signal shifted to t+1]
    E --> F[Equal-weighted sector aggregation]
    G[FRED: CPI, FEDFUNDS, GDP, GS10] --> H[Dynamic long/short threshold]
    F --> I[Long/short decision per sector]
    H --> I
    I --> J[Portfolio P&L]
    F --> K[Risk metrics<br/>Sharpe, vol, drawdown, alpha]
    F --> L[Recession stress test]
    J --> M[outputs/]
    K --> M
    L --> M
```

The pipeline runs as seven logged steps and writes everything to disk — nothing is printed and lost.

