## Quickstart

**Requirements:** Python 3.10+, a free [FRED API key](https://fred.stlouisfed.org/docs/api/api_key.html).

```bash
git clone <your-repo-url>
cd sector-rotation-ml

python -m venv .venv && source .venv/bin/activate   # Windows: .venv\Scripts\activate
pip install -r requirements.txt

cp .env.example .env    # then add your FRED_API_KEY
```

`.env.example`:

```
FRED_API_KEY=your_key_here
```

The pipeline refuses to start without a key rather than failing deep inside a request call. TA-Lib is **not** a dependency — all indicators are implemented in pandas, so there's no C library to compile.

**Run:**

```bash
python main.py \
  --initial-investment 100000000 \
  --start-date 2021-01-01 \
  --end-date 2024-01-31
```

First run downloads ~40 tickers and caches them as parquet under `cache/`; subsequent runs with the same date range hit the cache instead of Yahoo Finance.

